# Alter Ego SFTP deploy (shared hosting)

This rule covers the **SFTP shared-hosting** deploy path. For the Docker/Coolify
VPS path on `server.masche.at` (different infrastructure), see `doc/deploy-vps.md`
and the user-level **`server-masche-deploy`** skill. The same local
`~/.ssh/id_ed25519` key is used for both (key setup/regeneration is documented in
that skill).

## Deploy config: `.env.deploy.local`

Gitignored, read by `scripts/push-live.mjs`, `pull-live.mjs`,
`pull-live-data.mjs`. Required keys:

| Variable | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `DEPLOY_SSH_HOST` | SFTP host |
| `DEPLOY_USER` | SSH user |
| `DEPLOY_PATH` | Remote web root (default `public_html`) |
| `SSH_KEY_PATH` | Absolute path to private key (`~/.ssh/id_ed25519`) |
| `SSH_KEY_PASSPHRASE` | Leave empty for the unattended key |
| `DEPLOY_PUBLIC_URL` | Public site URL (default `https://www.braincell.online`) |

## Usage

- Deploy app + data: `npm run deploy:live` (builds, then SFTP push).
- Deploy app only (skip compendium DB): `npm run deploy:live:app`.
- Pull live state back: `npm run pull:live`.
- Auth is key-based SFTP; if a push fails with auth errors, confirm the public
  key is in the server `authorized_keys` and `SSH_KEY_PATH` points at the
  matching private key.
